# Operator credentials. Copy to `.env.local` and fill in; `.env.local` is gitignored.
#
# WHAT GOES HERE: values a PERSON uses from a shell to operate the deployed project.
# WHAT NEVER GOES HERE: anything the app reads. The app's two values — the project URL and the
# publishable key — live in `challange-5/Config/Backend.xcconfig`, are written into the bundle as
# `Backend.plist` by a build phase, and are public by design (RLS is what protects the data).
#
# The service-role key BYPASSES RLS ENTIRELY. `docs/backend-supabase.md` §8 and
# `.claude/plans/supabase/c2-wiring/03-security-privacy.md` §1 put it in exactly two places: an Edge
# Function's environment, and CI secrets. A third copy on a laptop is a fourth place it can leak
# from, so keep this file only while a drill needs it and delete it afterwards.
#
# This project has already had one production key exposure and rotation. That is the precedent.

# Project: Histoplora (ppwcxmvetmmwliusliac, ap-southeast-1)
SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF=ppwcxmvetmmwliusliac
SUPABASE_URL=https://ppwcxmvetmmwliusliac.supabase.co

# From the dashboard: Project Settings -> API Keys -> service_role / secret key.
# Used only to call `publish-suppressions`, which refuses any other bearer (`c2` blocker B7).
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Optional: a personal access token, if a CLI command asks for one.
SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=
